    "title": "FINAL: LSU beats Texas A&M 35-6 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Hunter McCann ,\n7 hours ago BATON ROUGE - LSU bounced back against Texas A&M on Saturday night after suffering a 32-24 road loss to Ole Miss last week. LSU struck first on its second drive of the game as running back Dilin Jones broke off a 36-yard run to move the Tigers to the edge of the Texas A&M red zone. Just a few plays later, Jones took a direct snap across the goal line to give LSU an early 7-0 lead. Read full article",
